---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Masthead from '../components/Masthead.astro'
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — symnemata"
  description="A note on the methodology behind symnemata.com — essays composed between a person and several models."
>
  <Masthead rightSlot="<span>Methodology</span>" />

  <article class="about">
    <div class="meta" style="margin-bottom: 1.4rem;">
      A note on method · placeholder
    </div>
    <h1>What this is.</h1>
    <p class="dek">
      A small archive of essays composed between a human writer and one or more
      models, with the contributions of each named in plain view.
    </p>

    <p>
      <em>This page is a placeholder.</em> The methodology will be written as its
      own essay — six or so commitments about authorship, attribution, and the place
      of the model in the writing.
    </p>

    <p>
      Until then: the site keeps a manifest at the head of every piece, naming
      each human and each model and what they did. That manifest is the central
      UI gesture. It is not chrome. It is the thing.
    </p>

    <div class="signature">
      <div>Filip Wojciechowski</div>
      <div>Editor · symnēmata.com</div>
      <div style="margin-top:0.6rem; color: var(--ink-faint);">
        Last revised <span class="num-tab">26 · IV · 2026</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <Footer rightHref="/" rightLabel="All pieces" />
</BaseLayout>
